# A1/A1.2/A1_12_family_and_appearance.letz
# Source: PDF slide deck "L3 (Part 1) a1convlotsmanmeli.pdf" (A1 Conversation course, Lesson 3, Part 1)
# Source: PDF slide deck "L3 (Part 2) a1convlotsmanmeli.pdf" (A1 Conversation course, Lesson 3, Part 2)
# (m)/(f)/(n)/(pl) markers stripped; nouns given in definite-article form.
# "Bréll" corrected to "Brëll" per LOD; glossed "the eyeglasses" to disambiguate
#   from "Glieser = glasses" (drinking glasses) taught in A1.1/A1_07.
# Already taught elsewhere and reused only inside sentences/distractors here,
#   not re-taught as @word: kleng, grouss, al, nei, waarm, rout, gro, brong,
#   schwaarz, riicht, kuerz, laang, jonk, bestuet, d'Hoer, d'Kand/Kanner,
#   de Papp, d'Mamm, de Brudder, d'Schwëster, de Jong, d'Meedchen/Meedercher,
#   den Enkel, d'Duechter, d'Bomi.
# Fills added: 20 fills drilling negation (net / kee / keen / keng — the gender/number
#   contrast), possessive pronouns (mäi/meng/däi/deng), and predicative appearance
#   adjectives. Sentences added from Part 2: negation Q&A pairs, Beschreif d'Leit
#   descriptions (Jhemp, Madamm Peters, Néckel, Tunn). Word "muskuléis" added for
#   new sentence usage.

@lesson A1.12 "Family & Appearance"

# --- Family: parents & grandparents ---
@word d'Famill = the family
@word d'Familljen = the families
@word no Famill = close family
@word d'Grousselteren = the grandparents
@word d'Elteren = the parents
@word de Grousspapp = the grandfather
@word d'Grousspappen = the grandfathers
@word d'Groussmamm = the grandmother
@word d'Groussmammen = the grandmothers
@word de Bopa = the grandpa
@word d'Bopaen = the grandpas

# --- Family: siblings & extended family ---
@word d'Geschwëster = the siblings
@word de Monni = the uncle
@word d'Monnien = the uncles
@word d'Tatta = the aunt
@word d'Tattaen = the aunts
@word de Cousin = the cousin (male)
@word d'Cousinen = the cousins (male)
@word d'Cousine = the cousin (female)
@word d'Cousineën = the cousins (female)
@word den Neveu = the nephew
@word d'Neveuen = the nephews
@word d'Niess = the niece
@word d'Niessen = the nieces

# --- Family: in-laws ---
@word de Schwoer = the brother-in-law
@word d'Schwoeren = the brothers-in-law
@word d'Schwéiesch = the sister-in-law
@word d'Schwéieschen = the sisters-in-law
@word d'Schwéiermamm = the mother-in-law
@word de Schwéierpapp = the father-in-law
@word d'Schwéierelteren = the parents-in-law
@word den Eedem = the son-in-law
@word d'Eedemen = the sons-in-law
@word d'Schnauer = the daughter-in-law
@word d'Schnaueren = the daughters-in-law

# --- Appearance: body ---
@word d'A = the eye
@word d'Aen = the eyes
@word d'Nues = the nose
@word de Brëll = the eyeglasses
@word d'Glatz = the bald head

# --- Appearance: adjectives ---
@word déck = big, fat, thick
@word gekrauselt = curly
@word dënn = thin, skinny
@word kal = cold
@word sportlech = sporty
@word muskuléis = muscular
@word schwéier = difficult, heavy

# --- Life status & accessories ---
@word leedeg = single
@word de Piercing = the piercing

# --- Verbs ---
@word fëmmen = to smoke
@word beschreiwen = to describe

@sentence
@lu D'Sara ass meng Niess.
@en Sara is my niece.
@distractor-en aunt
@distractor-en cousin
@distractor-lu Tatta
@distractor-lu Cousine

@sentence
@lu De Robert ass mäi Schwoer.
@en Robert is my brother-in-law.
@distractor-en uncle
@distractor-en nephew
