# --- @fill: negation — net / kee / keen / keng --------------------------------
# Centrepiece drill: kee(n) for masc/neut singular, keng for fem singular + all
# plurals, net for verbs/adjectives/names/possessives/definite articles. The
# distractors are always the competing negation forms.

@fill
@lu Hatt ass [net] bestuet.
@en She is [not] married.
@distractor-lu kee
@distractor-lu keng
@distractor-lu keen
@distractor-en no
@distractor-en none
@distractor-en never

@fill
@lu Ech hu [kee] Jong.
@en I don't have a [son].
@distractor-lu keng
@distractor-lu net
@distractor-lu keen
@distractor-en daughter
@distractor-en brother
@distractor-en sister

@fill
@lu Ech hu [keng] Fra.
@en I don't have a [wife].
@distractor-lu kee
@distractor-lu net
@distractor-lu keen
@distractor-en husband
@distractor-en sister
@distractor-en mother

@fill
@lu Ech hu [keng] Geschwëster.
@en I don't have [siblings].
@distractor-lu kee
@distractor-lu net
@distractor-lu keen
@distractor-en children
@distractor-en parents
@distractor-en cousins

@fill
@lu Dat ass [net] meng Schwëster.
@en That is [not] my sister.
@distractor-lu kee
@distractor-lu keng
@distractor-lu keen
@distractor-en no
@distractor-en none
@distractor-en never

